+    <div class="panel">
+      <span class="eyebrow">Five mechanisms, not five promises</span>
+      <ol class="steps" style="margin-top:14px">
+        <li><span><b>Declared capability.</b> The policy engine checks the acting role, the action, and
+          the risk tier against the role's own contract. An action the role never declared is
+          refused even at maximum autonomy. The Explorer is read-only by a hard-coded rule, not by
+          convention.</span></li>
+        <li><span><b>Token-bound leases.</b> A worker claims a job with a lease token. If the lease
+          expires and another worker takes over, the first worker's write raises
+          <code>StaleLeaseError</code> instead of silently winning.</span></li>
+        <li><span><b>Write-scope conflict rules.</b> Two nodes whose write scopes overlap &mdash; by path
+          or by directory containment &mdash; must have a dependency between them, or the graph is
+          rejected before anything runs. Parallelism cannot produce a collision.</span></li>
+        <li><span><b>Mandatory consultation.</b> Scheduled work names at least two other roles to
+          consult, capped at three rounds, and a role can never be its own consultant. Eight
+          authority classes &mdash; credentials, legal, spend, production access, protected-branch
+          merge, owner value choices, personal consent, external commitments &mdash; escalate to a
+          human every time.</span></li>
