+
+  <h3 style="margin:34px 0 6px">What the planner refuses to accept</h3>
+  <p class="measure" style="margin:0 0 14px">Each row below is a graph that was actually submitted
+    to the validator while preparing this page, and the message it came back with. The plan is
+    rejected before a single node runs.</p>
+  <div class="tablewrap">
+    <table>
+      <thead><tr><th>Submitted graph</th><th></th><th>Validator response</th></tr></thead>
+      <tbody>
+        <tr><td class="k">Two nodes write the same file, no dependency between them</td><td><span class="state no">rejected</span></td><td class="mono">overlapping write scopes require a dependency</td></tr>
+        <tr><td class="k">One node writes a directory another writes a file inside</td><td><span class="state no">rejected</span></td><td class="mono">overlapping write scopes require a dependency</td></tr>
+        <tr><td class="k">Same two nodes, dependency edge restored</td><td><span class="state ok">accepted</span></td><td class="mono">&mdash;</td></tr>
+        <tr><td class="k">A dependency cycle</td><td><span class="state no">rejected</span></td><td class="mono">work graph contains a cycle</td></tr>
+        <tr><td class="k">A node depending on itself</td><td><span class="state no">rejected</span></td><td class="mono">work item cannot depend on itself</td></tr>
+        <tr><td class="k">Child depth that does not match its parent</td><td><span class="state no">rejected</span></td><td class="mono">work item depth does not match parent</td></tr>
+        <tr><td class="k">A charter acceptance spec no node covers</td><td><span class="state no">rejected</span></td><td class="mono">work graph is missing charter acceptance</td></tr>
+        <tr><td class="k">A ninth child under one parent</td><td><span class="state no">rejected</span></td><td class="mono">work graph exceeds fanout limit</td></tr>
+        <tr><td class="k">Node budgets summing past the mission charter</td><td><span class="state no">rejected</span></td><td class="mono">total consumptive schedule budget exceeds charter max_wall_seconds</td></tr>
+      </tbody>
+    </table>
+  </div>
+</section>
+
+<section id="problems">
+  <div class="shead">
+    <span class="eyebrow">Separable problems</span>
+    <h2>Seven different jobs, seven different entry points</h2>
+    <p class="measure">The pieces are not a single monolithic pipeline you have to adopt whole.
+      Each command below solves one problem on its own, with its own roles and its own artifact.
+      You can use the verifier and never run an agent; you can plan a graph and execute it
+      elsewhere.</p>
+  </div>
+
+  <div class="problems">
+    <article class="problem">
+      <h3>&ldquo;An agent changed my code. Did it do what it claims?&rdquo;</h3>
+      <p>Point the verifier at a commit and an acceptance specification that was written
+        <em>before</em> that commit. The spec must declare every path the commit touched; an
+        undeclared file fails the check. A passing run writes a bundle, a failing one writes
+        nothing.</p>
+      <div class="rr-wrap"><span class="rolerow"><span class="rr" style="background:var(--role-curator)"></span></span><span>curator only</span></div>
+      <pre>hive-mind verify \
+  --repository /path/to/repo \
+  --spec acceptance-spec.json \
+  --candidate &lt;40-hex sha&gt; \
+  --output ./receipt-bundle</pre>
+    </article>
+
+    <article class="problem">
+      <h3>&ldquo;Fix this, and prove it end to end.&rdquo;</h3>
+      <p>The full delivery loop: reproduce the failure, write the change on a branch, seal the
+        checks, re-run them independently, publish a reversible bundle. Runs offline against a
+        local repository; nothing is pushed anywhere.</p>
+      <div class="rr-wrap"><span class="rolerow"><span class="rr" style="background:var(--role-explorer)"></span><span class="rr" style="background:var(--role-builder)"></span><span class="rr" style="background:var(--role-curator)"></span></span><span>explorer · builder · curator</span></div>
+      <pre>hive-mind demo
+
+<span class="c"># or, against the fixture layout:</span>
+hive-mind deliver \
+  --backend fixture-demo</pre>
+    </article>
+
+    <article class="problem">
+      <h3>&ldquo;What state is this repository in, provably?&rdquo;</h3>
+      <p>Emits a digested audit of a Git worktree &mdash; repository facts, test results, and
+        source dockets &mdash; optionally HMAC-signed with a key that is never written into the
+        artifact. Skipping tests marks the audit incomplete rather than passing it.</p>
+      <div class="rr-wrap"><span class="rolerow"><span class="rr" style="background:var(--role-steward)"></span><span class="rr" style="background:var(--role-curator)"></span></span><span>steward · curator</span></div>
+      <pre>hive-mind audit \
+  --output evidence/state.json \
+  --signing-key-file KEY \
+  --signing-key-id k1</pre>
+    </article>
+
+    <article class="problem">
+      <h3>&ldquo;Many units of work, and they must not collide.&rdquo;</h3>
+      <p>Plan a bounded work DAG and read it back, event-derived. Overlapping write scopes must be
+        ordered, fanout is capped at eight, depth and budget are bounded by the charter. The graph
+        is rejected at plan time, not discovered at merge time.</p>
+      <div class="rr-wrap"><span class="rolerow"><span class="rr" style="background:var(--role-orchestrator)"></span></span><span>orchestrator</span></div>
+      <pre>hive-mind kernel plan &lt;mission&gt; \
+  --charter charter.json \
+  --fixture bugfix
+
+hive-mind kernel graph &lt;mission&gt; \
+  --charter charter.json --json</pre>
+    </article>
+
+    <article class="problem">
+      <h3>&ldquo;Drive a long campaign in a repo &mdash; without handing over credentials.&rdquo;</h3>
+      <p>Autopilot records an objective in the target repository and emits a host-neutral
+        orchestration contract: content-addressed task effects your own agent host executes inside
+        its own approved sandbox. It never creates the tasks itself, never touches a protected
+        branch, and fails closed if a different objective is submitted for the same request.</p>
+      <div class="rr-wrap"><span class="rolerow"><span class="rr" style="background:var(--role-orchestrator)"></span><span class="rr" style="background:var(--role-integrator)"></span></span><span>orchestrator · integrator</span></div>
+      <pre>hive-mind autopilot run \
+  "reduce checkout p95" \
+  --repository /path/to/repo</pre>
+    </article>
+
+    <article class="problem">
+      <h3>&ldquo;The machine died mid-run. Now what?&rdquo;</h3>
+      <p>Missions can be enqueued into a durable local SQLite scheduler with token-bound leases,
+        bounded retries, and dead-lettering, then resumed. A worker that lost its lease cannot
+        write over the one that took over.</p>
+      <div class="rr-wrap"><span class="rolerow"><span class="rr" style="background:var(--role-steward)"></span><span class="rr" style="background:var(--role-orchestrator)"></span></span><span>steward · orchestrator</span></div>
+      <pre>hive-mind enqueue --repository . \
+  --objective "…" \
+  --acceptance-spec spec.json
+
+hive-mind serve   <span class="c"># drain it</span>
+hive-mind resume  <span class="c"># pick it back up</span></pre>
+    </article>
+
+    <article class="problem">
+      <h3>&ldquo;Is the system actually improving, or does it just say so?&rdquo;</h3>
+      <p>Benchmarks and experiments compare a challenger against a sealed baseline. The Optimizer
+        may propose an immutable challenger variant and recommend it; the promotion decision is
+        somewhere else entirely, and a lesson with no cited evidence cannot acquire an identity.</p>
+      <div class="rr-wrap"><span class="rolerow"><span class="rr" style="background:var(--role-optimizer)"></span></span><span>optimizer</span></div>
+      <pre>hive-mind benchmark …
+hive-mind experiment …</pre>
+    </article>
+  </div>
+</section>
+
+<section id="use">
+  <div class="shead">
+    <span class="eyebrow">Getting started</span>
+    <h2>Sixty seconds, no network, no keys</h2>
+  </div>
+  <div class="grid2">
+    <div class="panel">
+      <span class="eyebrow">Step one</span>
+      <pre style="margin-top:12px">python -m pip install --no-deps -e .
+hive-mind demo</pre>
+      <p style="font-size:.88rem; margin:14px 0 0">Creates a throwaway repository with a known
+        regression, repairs it, verifies the repair independently, and writes the bundle to
+        <code>./demo-out</code>. The output directory must not already exist &mdash; the tool will
+        not overwrite evidence.</p>
+    </div>
+    <div class="panel">
+      <span class="eyebrow">Step two — read what it wrote</span>
+      <pre style="margin-top:12px">jq '.curator_verdict, .budget_consumption' \
+   demo-out/mission-report.json
+
+<span class="c">"adopt"</span>
+<span class="c">{ "compute_units": 45.0,</span>
+<span class="c">  "episodes": 15, "tool_calls": 45 }</span></pre>
+      <p style="font-size:.88rem; margin:14px 0 0">Then run
+        <code>python -m unittest discover -s tests -v</code> &mdash; the repository's own CI gate,
+        and the same command the Curator seals as a check.</p>
+    </div>
+  </div>
+</section>
+
+<section id="status">
+  <div class="shead">
+    <span class="eyebrow">Where it actually is</span>
+    <h2>The honest status table</h2>
+    <p class="measure">This project's own README leads with its limits, and this page would be
+      misrepresenting it if it did otherwise. Version 0.7.0 is a prototype. The verification
+      machinery is real and runs offline; the autonomous coding agent on top of it is not ready.</p>
+  </div>
+  <div class="tablewrap">
+    <table>
+      <thead><tr><th>Capability</th><th>State</th><th>What that means in practice</th></tr></thead>
+      <tbody>
+        <tr><td class="k">Verify a local change against sealed checks</td><td><span class="state ok">works</span></td><td>Offline and deterministic. <code>hive-mind verify</code>.</td></tr>
+        <tr><td class="k">Complete deterministic fixture delivery</td><td><span class="state ok">works</span></td><td>Offline. It repairs one bundled fixture layout — it is not a general coding agent.</td></tr>
+        <tr><td class="k">Bounded work-DAG planning and validation</td><td><span class="state ok">works</span></td><td>Deterministic digests; conflict, depth, fanout and budget rules all enforced.</td></tr>
+        <tr><td class="k">Durable queue, leases, resume</td><td><span class="state ok">works</span></td><td>Local SQLite. Survives a crash mid-mission.</td></tr>
+        <tr><td class="k">A real model driving the change</td><td><span class="state no">not ready</span></td><td><code>--backend model</code> is opt-in and experimental. Not for routine use.</td></tr>
+        <tr><td class="k">Remote push and pull requests</td><td><span class="state no">local only</span></td><td>Git operations stay on the local filesystem.</td></tr>
+        <tr><td class="k">Five of the eight roles</td><td><span class="state na">chartered</span></td><td>Orchestrator, Architect, Integrator, Steward, Optimizer have contracts and policy enforcement, no executable repository path yet.</td></tr>
+        <tr><td class="k">Hostile-code isolation</td><td><span class="state no">not claimed</span></td><td>Receipts record <code>posix-rlimit-only</code> enforcement. That is not a sandbox for adversarial code.</td></tr>
+        <tr><td class="k">Production use</td><td><span class="state no">no</span></td><td>Prototype release. No production use, no user validation yet.</td></tr>
+      </tbody>
+    </table>
+  </div>
+</section>
+
